    {
      "measure": "length_norm",
      "key": "additional_baselines.length_block_normalized",
      "label": "block-normalized (added 2026-10-21 before any run)",
      "description": "Length-only baseline on durations divided by the median go-window duration of the trial's own block: -|log((attempted / median of its block) / (imagined / median of its block))|; same rank statistics (length-matched and all). Imagined trials are ~1.5x longer than attempted ones, so the raw ratio favours long attempted trials rather than the proportionally matched one."
    }
  ],
  "implementation_choices": [
    "Go window = every bin from the go cue (meta go_offset) to the trial end.",
    "Trailing partial pooling window dropped: True.",
    "Cue TTS speech duration: speech_span on the TTS LPCNet c0 (threshold 30.0 dB below the loudest frame); no LPCNet synthesis.",
    "Length-matched candidates: ties in |TTS duration difference| go to the earlier attempted trial.",
    "Secondary similarity uses the unpooled go-window bins; length-only baseline uses go-window bins.",
    "Ranks: 1 = most similar; ties share the mid-rank; top-1 = rank exactly 1 (a tie for best is not top-1). Candidates with an undefined similarity would be left out (counted as n_undefined).",
    "p_perm = (1 + #{null mean rank <= observed}) / (1 + n_permutations), one-sided; the same draws give pooled and per-pair p; each measure x candidate set has its own seeded stream. p_exact: the same null by convolution (check).",
    "PCA axes from the covariance eigendecomposition of the standardized training frames; the projection uses the training mean and s.d. (no re-standardization of the components)."
  ],
